# Infra Notes — Behaviour_portal

## What to deploy
- Behaviour_portal (stripped ELF binary)
- flag.txt (real flag, one line)
- Dockerfile + docker-compose.yml

IMPORTANT:
- Do NOT ship flag.txt to players.
- The binary reads the real flag at runtime from ./flag.txt inside the container.

## Build & Run
From the challenge directory:

### Using Docker Compose
docker compose build
docker compose up -d

### Test
nc localhost 1337

## Session time limit (5 minutes)
The container should enforce per-connection timeouts:
- Use: timeout 300 ./Behaviour_portal
- socat must exec the binary through timeout.

## Recommended hardening
- Run as non-root user (ctf)
- read-only filesystem
- drop all capabilities
- no-new-privileges
- tmpfs for /tmp and /run
- resource limits (pids/mem/cpu)

## Scale guidance
- One port supports many concurrent clients.
- socat uses fork → one process per connection.
- Ensure pids_limit is high enough (>= expected concurrent players, e.g. 256).
- Ensure host ulimit for open files is sane (infra side).
